{#- CRS328 — guest turn-up DELTA: tag VLAN 30 on the AP uplink ports.
    Guest SSID frames ride the AP's tagged uplink (ether1); a switch AP-port
    carrying only VLAN 10/20 DROPS the guest tagged frames at ingress (the
    phone-disconnect / no-DHCP signature). The converge derives the same set
    from SSOT (wifi_ports + network_vlans ssid); this is the delta equivalent.
    VLAN 30 already exists as a trunk-only row, so SET it — an add fails with
    'vlan already added'. Idempotent: only sets when tagged~ether11 is absent. -#}
# =============================================================================
# Guest VLAN — CRS328 switch AP-port VLAN 30 tagged DELTA
# =============================================================================

:if ([/interface bridge vlan find where bridge=bridge vlan-ids=30 and tagged~"ether11"] = "") do={
    /interface bridge vlan set [find where vlan-ids=30] \
        tagged=bridge,sfp-sfpplus1,ether11,ether12 \
        comment="Guest VLAN on trunk (+ wifi AP ports tagged)"
}

# ---- End ----
# Verify: /interface bridge vlan print -> vlan-ids=30 tagged=bridge,sfp-sfpplus1,ether11,ether12